/*--------------------------------*- Choupo -*-----------------------*\
  combined02_brayton_rankine_shaft  --  a FULL Brayton cycle with a
  SHAFT-SPLIT node, and a DRY steam bottoming loop.
  =================================================================

  WHAT THIS CASE IS ABOUT: the SHAFT NODE.  combined01 wires one turbine to
  one generator.  Here a real compressor sits on the gas-turbine shaft, and a
  single `electricLoad` SUMS two work inputs:

      gasGenerator.W = gasTurbine.shaft (+gross)  +  compressor.shaft (-load)

  (Both rotating units publish a `shaft` port with expression "-W_shaft";
   the turbine's W_shaft<0 -> +, the compressor's W_shaft>0 -> -, so the
   generator nets to the delivered power: 1500 - 900 = 600 kW of shaft,
   582 kW of electricity at eta 0.97.)

      airFuelFeed (1 bar) -> compressor (-> ~8.3 bar) -> gibbsCombustor (1300 K)
        -> gasTurbine -> exhaust -> HRSG hot side -> flue
                 |  \                                   |
              (shaft) (shaft)                       (counter)
                 |     \                                |
            compressor  gasGenerator(net)      steamFeed (DRY, 5 bar 500 K)
                                                    -> heatedSteam
                                                    -> steamTurbine -> steamGenerator
                                                    -> steamCooler -> condensate

  -- WHAT THIS CASE DOES NOT MODEL, and it is not a detail -----------------

  THERE IS NO PHASE CHANGE ANYWHERE IN THIS PLANT.  The bottoming loop is fed
  SUPERHEATED STEAM (5 bar, 500 K -- 77 K above the 422.7 K saturation
  temperature this package's own vapour-pressure curve gives at 5 bar), not
  boiler feedwater.  So there is no economiser, no evaporator, no condenser
  and no feed pump: the "HRSG" here is a SUPERHEATER, and the loop is open,
  not a closed Rankine cycle.  Every stream in the plant is a gas and every
  `phase gas;` label in 0/ is true of the state it labels.

  WHY, and the numbers are measured on this flowsheet rather than argued.
  `heatExchanger` is an eps-NTU RATING model for SENSIBLE heat -- its own
  header says "sensible heat only, no phase change" -- so its cold-side
  capacity rate for a liquid feed is the LIQUID one, C = n.Cp_liq.  The most
  it can then deliver, at effectiveness 1, is

      Q/n  =  Cp_liq . (T_hot_in - T_cold_in)
           =  75.5 . (871.77 - 400)  =  35 561 J/mol        [measured: 355.61 kW / 10 mol/s]

  while water entering as liquid at 400 K / 5 bar needs

      h_g(Tsat) - h_l(400 K)  =  41 138 J/mol               [measured from this package]

  to reach the far side of the dome.  It is 5 577 J/mol SHORT, so the water
  stops INSIDE the dome, where this model has no two-phase outlet to write --
  it lands on the saturated-vapour line and 55.77 kW of latent heat is
  charged to nobody.  The exchanger says so in its own words ("closes in Q
  but not in H") and publishes the number as `H_closure_gap_kW`; declaring
  the feed as the liquid it would really be leaves this plant missing its
  first law by 13.5 % of its boundary energy.

  It is not a pressure that can be chosen better.  The eps-NTU duty above is
  355.61 kW at 3, 10 AND 20 bar -- identical, because it is set by the liquid
  capacity rate and the two inlet temperatures and by nothing else -- while
  the dome gets MORE expensive with pressure (42 068 J/mol at 10 bar,
  measured).  At 20 bar the exchanger stops on the LIQUID side of the dome
  instead and the plant misses by 12.0 %.  At 3 bar it stops on the
  saturation line at 405.1 K, the steam turbine's fixed 50 kW then discharges
  at 257.7 K, and the sensible-only `steamCooler` cannot take its declared
  45 kW out of that: the run stops at exit 2, `failed to converge`.  For this
  hardware the gas-turbine exhaust would have to reach about 946 K; the
  compressor on the shaft takes 900 kW out of the cycle and it leaves at
  871.8 K.

  WHERE THE PHASE CHANGE LIVES, then:
    * rankine02_water          -- a CLOSED Rankine on IAPWS-IF97: pump,
                                  dome-crossing `boiler`, turbine,
                                  dome-crossing `condenser`, tear stream.
                                  This is the steam-table truth.
    * combined01_brayton_rankine -- its HRSG DOES evaporate its feedwater
                                  (400 K liquid -> 803.3 K superheated
                                  vapour, 550.73 kW, first law closed to
                                  4e-8 kW), because its gas turbine leaves at
                                  1130.6 K and clears the dome with room to
                                  spare.  Its OWN header still calls that
                                  loop "gas-only, no phase change"; that
                                  sentence predates the 2026-09-08 exchanger
                                  enthalpy-inversion and is stale.  Believe
                                  the run, not the prose -- and the same
                                  warning applies to this paragraph.

  HISTORY, kept because it is the lesson.  0/steamFeed used to declare
  `T 400 K; phase gas;` -- at 5 bar that fluid is 23 K BELOW its dew point, a
  liquid wearing a vapour label.  The plant then violated the first law by
  21.07 % of its boundary energy, at exit 0, with a golden master pinning the
  answer: the latent heat of a phase change nobody had declared and nothing
  could charge.  No golden could have found it -- a golden pins what a run
  PRINTS, and a stable wrong answer passes one by construction.  What found
  it was `check_energy_closure`, which reads the residual instead.

  Global first-law residual, this run: -0.00021 kW (-7.3e-6 % of boundary
  energy exchanged) -- the plant closes.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

// stream state lives on disk in 0/ (per-stream files); flowsheetDict is TOPOLOGY only

units
(
    {
        name        compressor;
        type        compressor;
        in          airFuelFeed;
        outputs     ( compressedFeed );
        operation   { W_shaft 900.0 kW;  eta 0.82; }
        energyOutputs
        (
            { name shaft;  kind work;  expression "-W_shaft";  unit W; }
        );
    }
    {
        name        gibbsCombustor;
        type        gibbsReactor;
        in          compressedFeed;
        outputs     ( flueGasHot );
        operation
        {
            T          1300.0 K;
            P          8.0 bar;
            elements   ( C  H  O  N );
            species
            (
                { name  CH4;    atoms  ( 1  4  0  0 ); }
                { name  O2;     atoms  ( 0  0  2  0 ); }
                { name  N2;     atoms  ( 0  0  0  2 ); }
                { name  CO2;    atoms  ( 1  0  2  0 ); }
                { name  water;  atoms  ( 0  2  1  0 ); }
            );
        }
    }
    {
        name        gasTurbine;
        type        turbine;
        in          flueGasHot;
        outputs     ( gasTurbExhaust );
        operation   { W_shaft -1500.0 kW;  eta 0.85; }
        energyOutputs
        (
            { name shaft;  kind work;  expression "-W_shaft";  unit W; }
        );
    }
    {
        name        hrsg;
        type        heatExchanger;
        inputs      ( gasTurbExhaust  steamFeed );
        outputs     ( gasFlueWarm     heatedSteam );
        operation   { area 50.0 m2;  U 120.0 W/m2/K;  flow counter; }
    }
    {
        name        steamTurbine;
        type        turbine;
        in          heatedSteam;
        outputs     ( steamExhaust );
        operation   { W_shaft -50.0 kW;  eta 0.85; }
        energyOutputs
        (
            { name shaft;  kind work;  expression "-W_shaft";  unit W; }
        );
    }
    {
        name        steamCooler;
        type        heater;
        in          steamExhaust;
        outputs     ( steamCondensate );
        operation   { Q -45.0 kW; }
    }

    // --- SHAFT-SPLIT: the gas generator nets turbine(+) minus compressor(-) -
    {
        name        gasGenerator;
        type        electricLoad;
        operation   { eta 0.97; }
        energyInputs
        (
            { from gasTurbine.shaft;   kind work;  target W_shaft; }   // +gross
            { from compressor.shaft;   kind work;  target W_shaft; }   // -load (sum)
        );
    }
    {
        name        steamGenerator;
        type        electricLoad;
        operation   { eta 0.97; }
        energyInputs
        (
            { from steamTurbine.shaft;  kind work;  target W_shaft; }
        );
    }
);
